@@ -1,5 +1,7 @@
 # Future released-evidence methods — prepared source only
 
+The shared `fixture_url.py` metadata classifier permits only the exact disposable in-process negative-authentication test URL reconstructed from hash-pinned public source AST constants. It proves `TestClient(app)` uses its default origin and verifies the imported endpoint prefix source; it makes no app import, request or authentication change. Both scanners continue to reject every other sensitive URL and examine every match independently. The final22 pure positive/negative controls, two already-public original-log metadata matches and source-chain proof are selected explicitly, with the preserved first Prior packaging failure and before-method sources. All original log bytes remain unchanged; no fixture values are emitted in the metadata receipts. This narrow evidence exception is not production authentication or release acceptance.
+
 `build-released-evidence.py` and `verify-released-evidence-https.py` are prepared methods. Their creation does not run them, establish a gate result, create a public prefix, commit, push or publish a release. Root review and actual release/deployment inputs remain required. Existing `.task-evidence/front-office-decision-2246/review` stays unchanged.
 
 The builder creates only the previously absent `.task-evidence/front-office-decision-2246/released` in the clean `evidence/cache-string-sharing-2237` worktree. It requires an explicitly reviewed current evidence HEAD and the reviewed SHA256 of the actual root-authored R3 `source.json`. Final candidate/tree are loaded from those actual bytes at invocation; no new candidate is inferred from the preparation templates. The input must identify the new source superseding historical b602. It reads local originals and Git objects, uses no network or Docker, touches no source or controller files, and performs no commit/push. Missing, failed, stale or inconsistent mandatory inputs stop preparation. All checks precede atomic creation of the new prefix.
